            <div xml:id="d240-a1">

                <pb facs="0487" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg431"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From El Comercio, August 21, 1876, evening
                    edition.—Translation.]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Republic to the
                        people of Lima:</hi></p>
                <p>Yesterday a political reunion, being called by various citizens, was realized;
                    when finished, a part of the people, led astray by bad instigations, commenced
                    to commit disorderly acts, which I highly reprove and condemn, and which I will
                    suppress with firmness if unfortunately there is any attempt of their
                    repetition.</p>
                <p>Inhabitants of Lima, continue without fear your ordinary occupations; the
                    government watches over your tranquillity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1876-08-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 21, 1876</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MARIANO I. PRADO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
